try it with `npm install && npm run test`
then `npm install jquery@3.2.1 && npm run test`

Ok, here are my test results:

`$html = $('<form data-abide novalidate></form>').appendTo('body');`

The issue starts at the `append` and `domManip` method.
There we have `scripts = jQuery.map( getAll( fragment, "script" ), disableScript );`
A short test yields that `getAll( fragment, "script" ).length` is `0`.
In `jQuery.map` we use `if ( isArrayLike( elems ) ) {` which contains
```javascript
var length = !!obj && "length" in obj && obj.length,
	type = toType( obj );

if ( isFunction( obj ) || isWindow( obj ) ) {
	return false;
}
```

`console.log(type, isFunction( obj ))` results in `object true`.

Reverting it to
```javascript
var length = !!obj && "length" in obj && obj.length,
	type = toType( obj );

if ( type === "function" || isWindow( obj ) ) {
	return false;
}
```

fixes it

